Recommends:
 xnote,
 norvi-archive-keyring
Provides: xnote-placement
Description: GNOME Shell extension that puts XNote sticky notes back where they were
 XNote is a native Wayland application, and Wayland gives a client no way to
 place its own window: no position, no monitor, no workspace. This extension
 is the compositor side of that job. It remembers where each XNote note was
 -- position, monitor and workspace -- and puts it back every time the note
 opens, keyed by the note's title and stored under ~/.local/state.
 .
 After installing, log out and back in once, then enable it with
 `gnome-extensions enable xnote-placement@spencercnorton.github.io`.
